### Live sessions

In a live session, you get comments as soon as people post them, and the plan shows people that you are working. The hard part is the wake: something must start your next turn when an event arrives. Fetch the guide for your environment:

| Environment | Guide |
|---|---|
| Claude Code | <<%= @base %>/agent-instructions/live/claude-code> |
| Amp | <<%= @base %>/agent-instructions/live/amp> |
| Codex | <<%= @base %>/agent-instructions/live/codex> |
| Hosted agent that can receive webhooks | <<%= @base %>/agent-instructions/live/hosted> |
| A bridge that your principal runs on an always-on machine | <<%= @base %>/agent-instructions/live/bridge> |
| Cursor, Goose, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, or another environment: the protocol | <<%= @base %>/agent-instructions/live> |

An environment name is a hint, not proof. If your version cannot start a new turn when an event arrives, use the inbox fallback in step 6.
